{"id":"SEC-001","category":"security","criterion":"input_validation","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/evals/harness/ablation-grade.sh","line":549,"code_snippet":"for l in reversed(lines):\n    m = SUMMARY_RX.match(l.strip())","reasoning_trace":"Traced hidden_tests from run_suite (:1080) back to parse_pytest (:546): the summary and the -rA outcome lines are read from the stdout of a process that imports agent-authored code (any conftest.py or ini file the agent adds at rootdir is not in grader_protected). Reproduced on this host with the grader's exact argv: a conftest pytest_unconfigure hook printed 'PASSED …' lines and '===== 2 passed in 0.01s =====' after two real failures and called os._exit(0); the grader's regex picked passed=2, rc=0. A root pyproject.toml with addopts='-p no:terminal' removed pytest's own output entirely, leaving bad empty, so all_pass is true. Dissent DISS-C-001 reaches the same conclusion by a different route (python_files/--ignore-glob overrides).","finding":"Hidden-test results are forgeable by agent-authored code running inside the test process; hidden_tests, all_pass and verdict_accuracy trust unauthenticated stdout.","critique":"The restore of grader_protected only covers files the task lists; the agent can add conftest.py / pyproject.toml / tox.ini / setup.cfg at rootdir and hook pytest_configure/pytest_unconfigure or atexit. The last-match summary parse and the absence of any cross-check between summary counts and outcome lines make the forgery trivial.","remediation":"Before running the hidden suite, delete every conftest.py, pytest.ini, pyproject.toml, setup.cfg, tox.ini (and *.pth) in the tree that is not in the fixture or the overlay; run with -c /dev/null (or --override-ini) so only grader-chosen options apply; write results with --junitxml to a grader-chosen file and cross-check against the summary (mismatch → parse_error); count only overlay-destination node ids and treat a missing hidden node as failed. Add a bats case