{"id":"SEC-001","category":"security","criterion":"input_validation","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/evals/harness/ablation-grade.sh","line":549,"code_snippet":"for l in reversed(lines):\n    m = SUMMARY_RX.match(l.strip())","reasoning_trace":"Traced hidden_tests from run_suite (:1080) back to parse_pytest (:546): the summary and the -rA outcome lines are read from the stdout of a process that imports agent-authored code (any conftest.py or ini file the agent adds at rootdir is not in grader_protected). Reproduced on this host with the grader's exact argv: a conftest pytest_unconfigure hook printed 'PASSED …' lines and '===== 2 passed in 0.01s =====' after two real failures and called os._exit(0); the grader's regex picked passed=2, rc=0. A root pyproject.toml with addopts='-p no:terminal' removed pytest's own output entirely, leaving bad empty, so all_pass is true.","finding":"Hidden-test results are forgeable by agent-authored code running inside the test process; hidden_tests, all_pass and verdict_accuracy trust unauthenticated stdout.","critique":"The restore of grader_protected only covers files the task lists; the agent can add conftest.py / pyproject.toml / tox.ini / setup.cfg at rootdir and hook pytest_configure/pytest_unconfigure or atexit. The last-match summary parse and the absence of any cross-check between summary counts and outcome lines make the forgery trivial.","remediation":"Before running the hidden suite, delete every conftest.py, pytest.ini, pyproject.toml, setup.cfg, tox.ini (and *.pth) in the tree that is not in the fixture or the overlay; write results with --junitxml to a grader-chosen file and cross-check against the summary (mismatch → parse_error); count only overlay-destination node ids; require the summary's passed+failed+… to equal len(order). Add a bats case with a forging conftest that must grade 0/N.","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/807.html","https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/345.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-002","category":"security","criterion":"input_validation","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/evals/harness/ablation-grade.sh","line":1080,"code_snippet":"res = run_suite(final, t.test_command, t.static_cases)\ng[\"hidden_tests\"] = summary(res)","reasoning_trace":"test_command is a directory sweep (tests/) per the seeders (:397, :465) and the fixtures; the result is reported whole as hidden_tests. AG-1 (ablation-grade.bats:243) expects 7/7 for a hidden file of 5 cases because tests/test_existing.py is swept in; TASK.md tells the agent to add a test of its own (seed_tasks.py:432).","finding":"hidden_tests counts visible and agent-added tests; hidden_test_pass_rate is agent-inflatable.","critique":"Confirmed review Changes Required §2.","remediation":"Keep only order/bad entries whose path is an overlay destination (excluding structural); total = max(len(kept), static_cases).","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/807.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-003","category":"devops","criterion":"portability","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/evals/harness/ablation-grade.sh","line":714,"code_snippet":"tf.extractall(tree, filter=keep)","reasoning_trace":"hasattr(tarfile, 'data_filter') is False on this host's Python 3.11.2; extractall(filter=) raises TypeError, caught at :1290 as exit 2 for every run with a REVIEW/AUDIT verdict. Confirmed review Changes Required §1.","finding":"Snapshot extraction needs Python >= 3.11.4; on older interpreters every gated arm is ungradeable (arm-correlated hole).","remediation":"Feature-check at start or implement the member checks by hand and call extractall(members=…) without filter=; pick -P only when sys.version_info >= (3, 11).","confidence":"high","references":["https://docs.python.org/3/library/tarfile.html#extraction-filters","https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1104.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-004","category":"code_quality","criterion":"correctness","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/evals/harness/ablation-grade.sh","line":864,"code_snippet":"fp = f.get(\"file\") or f.get(\"path\")\nln = f.get(\"line\") or f.get(\"line_start\") or f.get(\"start_line\")","reasoning_trace":"Every finding in grimoires/loa/a2a/sprint-1/adversarial-review.json carries anchor '<file>:<symbol>', anchor_type 'function' and integer anchor_line; none has file/path/line. envelope_texts therefore emits only the symbol anchor, which citations() cannot parse. Confirmed review Changes Required §3.","finding":"Loa's own dissent envelope shape yields no citations; dissent-only catches earn zero recall.","remediation":"When anchor matches ^(?P<file>[^:]+):(?P<sym>[A-Za-z_]\\w*)$ and anchor_line is an int, emit f'{file}:{anchor_line}[-{anchor_line_end}]'; accept anchor_line as a line key.","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/20.html"]}
{"id":"DO-001","category":"devops","criterion":"test_portability","severity":"MEDIUM","score":2,"file":"head/evals/tests/ablation-grade.bats","line":16,"code_snippet":"BATS_BIN=\"$HOME/.local/dotfiles/tools/diff-so-fancy/test/bats/bin/bats\"","reasoning_trace":"Symlinked into the stub PATH at :48; on any other machine the link dangles, bats execs 127 inside the stub, and AG-2 (:268) and AG-7 (:352) fail. The review rated this HIGH; the audit calibrates it MEDIUM (test evidence lost, no production path).","finding":"Test depends on one operator's dotfiles path.","remediation":"BATS_BIN=\"${LOA_TEST_BATS:-$(command -v bats || true)}\" and skip when empty; same for /usr/bin/python3 at :46.","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1104.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-005","category":"security","criterion":"resource_limits","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/evals/harness/ablation-grade.sh","line":506,"code_snippet":"full = [A.docker_bin, \"run\", \"--rm\", \"--network\", \"none\", \"--read-only\", \"--tmpfs\", \"/tmp:rw,size=256m\", \"--user\", …]","reasoning_trace":"The container runs agent-authored test code. The argv has no --pids-limit, --memory, --cpus, --cap-drop ALL or --security-opt no-new-privileges; docker-stub.sh:56 lists --pids-limit/--memory/--cpus as flags the pipeline's own docker run uses, so the grader is the only unlimited run in the pipeline. The outer subprocess timeout (:518) kills only the docker client; no --name means no docker kill, so the container keeps the rw mount.","finding":"Grading container has no process, memory or CPU limits and no cleanup path on client timeout.","remediation":"Add --pids-limit 256 --memory 1g --cpus 1 --cap-drop ALL --security-opt no-new-privileges and a --name <uuid>; on TimeoutExpired run docker kill <name>.","confidence":"medium","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/400.html","https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/770.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-006","category":"security","criterion":"file_handling","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/evals/harness/ablation-grade.sh","line":242,"code_snippet":"os.chmod(os.path.join(r, d), 0o700)","reasoning_trace":"os.walk(followlinks=False) still lists symlinks to directories in ds; os.chmod follows them. copy_tree preserves agent symlinks verbatim (:283, :294), so grading/final holds them and a re-grade (fresh_dir :1041) or a protected-dir restore (put_file :306) chmods the link target — any grader-owned directory. Confirmed dissent DISS-C-001 / review Observations §2.","finding":"remove_path chmods through agent-planted symlinks, violating the stated write boundary.","remediation":"Skip os.path.islink(p) entries before chmod (or use os.chmod(..., follow_symlinks=False) where supported).","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/59.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-001","category":"code_quality","criterion":"correctness","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/evals/harness/ablation-grade.sh","line":1087,"code_snippet":"prepare(t, base_tree)\nif t.regression_command is not None:\n    rb = run_suite(base_tree, t.regression_command)","reasoning_trace":"The hidden overlay lands before regression_command runs on base and final; a regression command sweeping the overlay directory counts hidden cases, which fail at base by design, so --self-check base fails a correct task.","finding":"Regression suite runs after the hidden overlay.","remediation":"Run regression_command on copies taken before the overlay, or restore only grader_protected for that run.","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/670.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-002","category":"code_quality","criterion":"correctness","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/evals/harness/ablation-grade.sh","line":653,"code_snippet":"return res[\"passed\"] >= res[\"total\"] and not res[\"bad\"] and not res[\"parse_error\"]","reasoning_trace":"rc and timed_out are recorded (:638) but not consulted; a suite killed after printing a passing summary (rc 124) still counts as all_pass for verdict accuracy (:1129) and suite_green (:1105).","finding":"all_pass ignores rc and timed_out.","remediation":"Require rc == 0 and not timed_out.","confidence":"medium","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/754.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-003","category":"code_quality","criterion":"consistency","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/evals/harness/ablation-grade.sh","line":492,"code_snippet":"pre = [\"python3\", \"-P\"] if host else [\"python3\", \"-I\", \"-s\"]","reasoning_trace":"The seeders prove tasks with plain python3 -m pytest (seed_tasks.py:206-208, cwd importable); the grader strips cwd from sys.path. A seeded task whose tests import by cwd passes its proof and grades 0/N in every arm.","finding":"Seeder proof and grader argv disagree on the import path.","remediation":"Share shape_command's argv with the seeder proof, or make --self-check reference a hard pre-freeze step.","confidence":"medium","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1068.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-004","category":"code_quality","criterion":"error_handling","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/evals/harness/ablation-grade.sh","line":1119,"code_snippet":"if not extract_snapshot(run_dir, label, idx.get(label), tree):\n    continue","reasoning_trace":"A gate whose feedback file exists but whose snapshot cannot be extracted leaves verdict_accuracy_per_gate[gate] null, which the header (:110-111) reserves for a gate that did not run; verdict.value can also be the literal 'none' (:1057-1060) against the header's APPROVED/CHANGES_REQUIRED/null.","finding":"Silent null on snapshot failure; undocumented 'none' verdict value.","remediation":"Record a reason (snapshot_missing: [label]) and map 'none' to null in verdict.","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/391.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-005","category":"code_quality","criterion":"correctness","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/evals/harness/ablation-grade.sh","line":964,"code_snippet":"if \"hidden\" in low:\n    return \"hidden\"","reasoning_trace":"Substring match flags rg --hidden, find -name '.hidden*', ls --hide and a Grep pattern of 'hidden' as contamination.","finding":"Contamination scan has routine false positives on the word 'hidden'.","remediation":"Match a path component ((^|/)hidden(/|$)) and exclude the --hidden flag.","confidence":"medium","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/185.html"]}
{"id":"ARCH-001","category":"architecture","criterion":"scope","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/evals/harness/validate-suite.sh","line":1,"reasoning_trace":"PR title and reviewer.md claim sixteen frozen tasks under grimoires/loa/evals/ablation-2.0/tasks/ and a freeze; the diff holds no grimoires/ file and no MANIFEST.sha256; VS-1 (validate-suite.bats:31-44) now derives its expected count from whatever is committed and cannot fail on a wrong count; no ## AC Verification section in the implementation report.","finding":"The tasks and the freeze the PR describes are not in the change; VS-1 no longer asserts a count.","remediation":"Include the task tree and MANIFEST.sha256 or state where they land; keep VS-1 asserting a fixed 16; add AC Verification.","confidence":"medium","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1059.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-006","category":"code_quality","criterion":"correctness","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/evals/harness/lib/seed_tasks.py","line":570,"code_snippet":"selected = cands[: a.select]","reasoning_trace":"Selection is fixed before building; a build-time skip (:593-597) or secret refusal (:588-592) consumes a slot and is not backfilled, contradicting both wrapper headers (seed-bugfix-tasks.sh:43-44, seed-refactor-tasks.sh:37-38).","finding":"--select N can write fewer than N tasks with exit 0.","remediation":"Iterate over cands until written + failed == a.select or the list is exhausted.","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1068.html"]}
{"id":"ARCH-002","category":"architecture","criterion":"maintainability","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/evals/harness/ablation-grade.sh","line":166,"code_snippet":"exec python3 -I - \"$SCRIPT_DIR\" \"$REPO_ROOT\" \"${EVAL_DOCKER_BIN:-docker}\" \"$@\" <<'PY'","reasoning_trace":"1130 lines of Python inside a bash heredoc; nothing lints or py_compiles it in CI; grade() (:1045-1142) and load_task() (:319-419) each ~100 lines. seed_tasks.py already shows the lib/ pattern.","finding":"Grader body is unlintable and over-long.","remediation":"Move to evals/harness/lib/ablation_grade.py; keep the .sh as the exec wrapper.","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1120.html"]}
