{"id":"SEC-008","category":"security","criterion":"configuration","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/evals/harness/seed-bugfix-tasks.sh","line":77,"code_snippet":"exec python3 -I \"$SCRIPT_DIR/lib/seed_tasks.py\" bugfix --repo-default \"$REPO_ROOT\" \\\n  --no-secrets \"$REPO_ROOT/evals/graders/no-secrets.sh\" \"$@\"","reasoning_trace":"argparse last-wins: a caller's --no-secrets '' after the wrapper's value disables secrets_clean (seed_tasks.py:503-504) silently; and when no-secrets.sh is absent, rc 127 is read as a secret hit (review LOW). Same at seed-refactor-tasks.sh:66.","finding":"The no-secrets scan can be switched off from the wrapper's argv and misreports an absent scanner as a secret.","remediation":"Reject a caller-supplied --no-secrets in the wrapper; check the scanner exists in the missing-tool loop; treat rc 127 as exit 2.","confidence":"medium","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/693.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-009","category":"security","criterion":"isolation","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/evals/harness/ablation-grade.sh","line":513,"code_snippet":"full = [\"env\", \"-i\", \"PATH=\" + os.environ.get(\"PATH\", \"/usr/bin:/bin\"), \"HOME=\" + home, …]","reasoning_trace":"--executor host runs agent-authored test code with the grader's uid, network and filesystem; the only isolation is env -i and a scratch HOME. The header documents the mode but the grader prints no warning and grade.json carries only executor_mode.","finding":"Host executor runs untrusted code unsandboxed without an explicit acknowledgement.","remediation":"Print a one-line warning on stderr in host mode and require --allow-host (or an env ack) outside the bats suite.","confidence":"medium","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/250.html"]}
